'''An ant''' is a joke [[block]] introduced in [[Java Edition 20w14∞]] that moves around when placed on top of black or white [[concrete]].

== Obtaining ==
An ant cannot be obtained as an item. It can be placed using commands such as {{cmd|fill}} or {{cmd|setblock}}, and naturally generates in the "{{cd|ant}}" dimension. It cannot be [[mined]] or [[exploded]].

=== Natural generation ===
A single ant naturally generates in the "{{cd|ant}}" dimension, where it begins moving immediately.

== Usage ==
An ant simulates {{w|Langton's ant}}. If placed on top of black or white [[concrete]], it moves in a deterministic pattern, turning the concrete underneath it into its other variation.

If two ant blocks collide, it merges into a single block. It cannot be pushed by [[piston]]s, and can replace [[bedrock]]. If the concrete beneath it is broken, it stops moving. If a block is in its way, it either pushes the block or destroys it.  

